---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Investor Overview — TruVector"
  description="TruVector is a checkpoint an AI system runs before it acts. The thesis, the founder, and how to request investor materials."
  path="/investors"
>

  <section class="room" style="padding-top:96px;padding-bottom:56px" aria-labelledby="inv-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investor overview</p>
      <h1 class="suite-title" id="inv-title" style="max-width:23ch">The checkpoint that decides whether an AI&rsquo;s information is good enough to act on.</h1>
      <hr class="rule--champagne" style="margin-top:32px" />
      <p class="hero-support" style="margin-top:28px">Before an AI system acts, TruVector checks where its information came from, whether the sources are really separate, and whether they agree. It returns Allow, Review or Block: an answer a machine can follow and a person can check.</p>
      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:36px">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#request">Request materials</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#thesis">Read the thesis</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section class="room" id="thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Thesis</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="thesis-title">The enterprise risk has moved, and the tooling has not.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:44px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">While AI systems only wrote text, a person read the output before anything happened. Now those systems file records, move money, change settings and call other systems on their own. The risk becomes operational and legal, and the human review step is exactly what was removed to make the automation worth it.</p>
          <p>The question stops being whether the AI said something wrong and becomes whether it acted on something wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>Almost all investment in this space improves the answers AI produces. Guardrails, evaluations and monitoring sit on either side of the model. Very little sits in the path of the action itself, and what does is a permission lookup, not a check on the information.</p>
          <p>TruVector sits in that path. It is infrastructure rather than an app, which makes it hard to displace once a system depends on it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room room--alt" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Founder</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="why-title">Measurement is the discipline, not a metaphor.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:44px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">TruVector is built and run by Michael Brandon Lane, from Johnson City, Tennessee.</p>
          <p>His training is in chemical engineering and chemistry, where a number is worth nothing until you can say how it was measured and within what error. That is the whole idea behind this product, applied to information instead of materials.</p>
          <ul class="facts" style="margin-top:24px">
            <li>B.S. Chemical Engineering, Virginia Tech</li>
            <li>M.S. Chemistry, University of North Carolina at Greensboro</li>
            <li>Co-inventor, WIPO patent 2019/143483, lithium battery separator technology</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>He designed and built TruVector and every other InTellMe product himself. The science behind it, Lane Vector, applies the math of chemical kinetics to how information and intent move.</p>
          <p>That means a short line between a decision and a shipped change, from a founder who has already taken a product from the lab into high-volume manufacturing.</p>
          <ul class="facts" style="margin-top:24px">
            <li>Sibling site &mdash; <a href="https://www.intellmeai.com/" rel="noopener">intellmeai.com</a></li>
            <li>Direct &mdash; <a href="mailto:brandon@intellmeai.com">brandon@intellmeai.com</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room" id="position" aria-labelledby="pos-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investment</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="pos-title">Self-funded so far. Raising a pre-seed round.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:62ch">InTellMe has been built without outside money. The round will fund TruVector research and development, the growth of the products built on the same work, and company operations.</p>
      <p class="reveal" style="max-width:62ch">Terms, structure and financials are in the investor materials.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room room--alt" id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <div class="suite">
      <p class="kicker">Request</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="request-title">Request investor materials.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:56ch">The technical brief, test protocol, roadmap, use of funds and IP position are sent after review.</p>

      <form class="form reveal" id="investor-form" method="post" action="/api/investor-request">
        <input type="hidden" name="_started" id="_started" value="" />
        <input type="hidden" name="found" value="truvector.science" />
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="company_website">Company website</label>
          <input type="text" id="company_website" name="company_website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">Name <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="organization">Organization</label>
          <input type="text" id="organization" name="organization" autocomplete="organization" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="role">Role</label>
          <input type="text" id="role" name="role" autocomplete="organization-title" />
        </div>
        <div class="field field--wide">
          <label for="want">What you are looking for</label>
          <select id="want" name="want">
            <option value="Technical brief" selected>Technical brief</option>
            <option value="Investor materials">Investor materials</option>
            <option value="Research correspondence">Research correspondence</option>
            <option value="Pilot conversation">Pilot conversation</option>
            <option value="Other">Other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field field--wide">
          <label for="message">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5"></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="field--wide actions" style="margin-top:8px">
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send request</button>
          <span class="caption">Or write directly to <a href="mailto:brandon@intellmeai.com?subject=TruVector%20materials">brandon@intellmeai.com</a>.</span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .form { display: grid; gap: 24px 32px; margin-top: 40px; max-width: 720px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .form { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .field { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .field--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .form label {
    font-family: var(--label); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--stone-text);
  }
  .req { letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: none; color: var(--stone-text); }
  .form input, .form select, .form textarea {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--smoked-bronze);
    color: var(--ivory);
    border: 1px solid var(--bronze-edge);
    border-radius: 1px;
    padding: 13px 14px;
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.4;
    min-height: 44px;
    transition: border-color var(--t-micro) var(--ease-lobby);
  }
  .form textarea { min-height: 120px; resize: vertical; }
  .form input:hover, .form select:hover, .form textarea:hover { border-color: var(--bronze-edge-hot); }
  /* Invalid state is carried by weight and an inset edge as well as by hue,
     so it is perceivable without distinguishing red from bronze. */
  .form input:user-invalid, .form textarea:user-invalid {
    border-color: var(--danger);
    box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--danger);
  }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
</style>

<script src="/form-timing.js" defer is:inline></script>
